 "question": "Compare WHERE and HAVING in SQL, and compare inner and left joins in pandas merge.",
 "answer": "WHERE clause in SQL filters individual rows before grouping, as per [S1]. HAVING clause filters whole groups after aggregation, as per [S1]. For joins, inner join in pandas merge keeps only matching keys from both tables, as per [S8]. Left join keeps every row of the left table and fills unmatched right-hand columns with NaN, as per [S8] [S9]. and [S10] provide additional context but do not directly compare WHERE and HAVING or joins. INSUFFICIENT_Evidence: left join in pandas merge is not compared to inner join. [S8]",
