  {
   "id": "S9",
   "kind": "document",
   "title": "Data Glossary",
   "text": "NULL: the SQL marker for a missing value.\nNaN: floating-point not-a-number used by pandas for missing numeric data.\nNone: Python's null object; pandas also treats None as missing in object columns.\nkey: the column or columns used to match rows when joining two tables.\nschema: the names and data types of the columns of a table.\nsample: DataFrame.sample(n=3) returns 3 random rows. It is a row draw, not a statistical sample design.\nmerge versus join: pd.merge joins on columns by default, whereas DataFrame.join joins on the index by default.\nindex: depends on context - database index, pandas Index or list position.",
