   "title": "Data Wrangling Handbook",
   "text": "2. Missing Values\npandas represents missing numbers as NaN. isna() flags them, dropna() removes rows with any\nmissing value by default, and fillna(value) replaces them. NaN is not equal to itself, so a\ncomparison such as x == np.nan is never true; use isna() instead.\nIn SQL the missing marker is NULL, and a comparison with NULL is unknown, so use IS NULL\nrather than = NULL. Aggregations such as AVG ignore NULL values; the pandas mean() skips\nNaN by default (skipna=True).",
